It is illegal to make access to a computer system without authorization
so as to delete data.  In fact, it's seriously illegal.

I think that it's only authorized to cancel a message if:

a) You posted it
b) It's posted in a newsgroup you have authority over (ie. you're a moderator)
c) Somebody else posted it, but you wrote it or you're acting for the
   person who wrote it.  (Ie. it's a copyright violation)
d) It violates USENET technical standards
e) It violates *universally* accepted posting standards.
f) You are otherwise authorized by each site you send the cancel to.
