[...]
>(As an example of what looks like evidence of incompetence to me,
>consider paragraph 3.3:

>   En bruker plikter å ikke gjøre brukeridentitet, passord eller
>   lignende sikkerhetselementer kjent for andre.

>loosely translated into English as

>   A user must not make user identity, password or similar security
>   elements known to others.
[...]

I've critiqued dozens of university computer polices and often see
similar silly "bugs". I don't see these bugs as evidence of
incompetent people, but rather as evidence of an incompetent
policy-creation process. In a good policy-creation process, many
people help debug a policy by reviewing and critiquing it.

One good way to do this is to post a draft of the policy to your local
newsgroup. At least for English-language policies, posting a draft
policy to comp.admin.policy (and alt.comp.acad-freedom.talk) also
seems valuable.

- Carl

