>Sorry for a stupid question, but what exactly is a "gay book"?

>Is that one that paints homosexuals in a favourable light, or is it any 
>book that mentions gays?

A "gay book" (also known as "happy book") is a book containing many
brightly-colored illustrations depicting generally playful and 
light-hearted subjects.  While these may also portray gays in a 
favorable light, no reference to gays or sexuality need be included
in a "gay book".  However, reflecting anything in a bad light is 
a concept foreign to the true "gay book" which is marketed on the
theory that "negativity is a no-no".  Many parents, fearing that 
children will not be properly encouraged to engage in vitriolic
