I'd like to make a few suggestions about how to handle the people afflicting
...I like to think of them as Net Pimples (NPs)...our kitty network:

  1) Everybody use a kill file, I know how to use one in the 'nn' reader but
     not the others. email me and I'll send you directions.

  2) If you must respond to these afflictions, please do not copy the offending
     message in your response. We would all do better if we never responded
     directly to the person since it is hard to for them to get their jollies
     if nobody is listening. If everybody used their kill files and never
     responded, the frequency of these afflicted peoples' postings would 
     decrease in my opinion.

  3) When you see an offensive post, respond to netcom, or mcs, or to the
     university, or the company's postmaster...once. Be polite, respectfully
     ask they investigate. I made a mistake in sending a note to mcs asking
     them to restrain an employee, I had no idea they were a net access
     company and forgot messages can be forged.

  4) Don't listen to the organization's postmaster if he complains to stop
     bothering them. Either they have respect for the internet and usenet
     (or whatever netnet) or we should have no respect for them. Keep sending
     those messages. Most universities will look into offending posts and most
     have policies to handle that sort of behavior. We expect nothing less
     from private companies.

The effect of the above suggestions (I hope) is that every Net Pimple will
cause one spate of irrate replies to the proper postmaster and then he will
cease to have a forum after that.

Gerry
